<article class="env-corollary" id="06MF">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06MF">Corollary <span data-tag="06MF">7.4.1.18</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a left fibration of $\infty $-categories which admits a covariant transport representation $\operatorname{Tr}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ and let $F: K^{\triangleleft } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a morphism of simplicial sets. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The composition $K^{\triangleleft } \xrightarrow {F} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\xrightarrow { \operatorname{Tr}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} } \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ is a limit diagram. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
Every lifting problem 
</p>
<div class="equation" id="06MG">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="06MG" href="/tag/06MG">7.56</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:improvement-scheme3} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ K \ar [r]^-{ \widetilde{F}_0} \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [d]^{U} \\ K^{\triangleleft } \ar [r]^-{F} \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur]^{ \widetilde{F} } &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p>
 admits a solution, where $\widetilde{F}$ is a $U$-limit diagram. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
<p> Moreover, if these conditions are satisfied, then every diagram $\widetilde{F}: K^{\triangleleft } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ satisfying $U \circ \widetilde{F} = F$ is a $U$-limit diagram. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Proposition <a data-tag="05R3" href="/tag/05R3">7.4.1.16</a>, we can reformulate condition $(1)$ as follows: 
    <p>
<dl>
<dt>$(1')$</dt>
<dd><p>
The restriction map $Q: \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( K^{\triangleleft }, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( K, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}})$ is a homotopy equivalence of Kan complexes. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl>
<p>
       Since $U$ is a left fibration, the morphism $Q$ is a left fibration between Kan complexes (Proposition <a data-tag="00TP" href="/tag/00TP">4.2.5.1</a>), and therefore a Kan fibration (Corollary <a data-tag="01NV" href="/tag/01NV">4.4.3.8</a>). In particular, $Q$ is a homotopy equivalence if and only if every fiber of $Q$ is a contractible Kan complex (Proposition <a data-tag="00X1" href="/tag/00X1">3.2.7.2</a>). We can therefore restate $(1')$ as follows: 
    <p>
<dl>
<dt>$(1'')$</dt>
<dd><p>
For every lifting problem of the form (<a data-tag="06MG" href="/tag/06MG">7.56</a>), the space of solutions 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( K^{\triangleleft }, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \times _{ \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( K, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) } \{  \widetilde{F}_0 \}  \]
</div>
<p>
 is a contractible Kan complex. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl>
<p>
       The desired result now follows from Corollary <a data-tag="06MD" href="/tag/06MD">7.1.6.15</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></p></p></article>
